  "id": "borna-disease",
  "term": "borna disease",
  "definition": "Borna disease is a sporadic neurological illness of horses and sheep caused by mammalian Borna disease virus. It occurs mainly in certain endemic parts of central Europe, tends to peak seasonally in spring, and evidence in the packet suggests the bicolored white-toothed shrew may act as a natural host that helps maintain the virus.",
